$ enola coverage --help
exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
Usage: enola coverage [flags] [repo_path|config_path]

Report which cross-repo edges enola resolved and which it could not, per service.
Tells a genuinely isolated service apart from one whose outbound edges enola simply
failed to follow — a distinction the graph alone cannot express.

Needs two or more repositories in one graph; point it at a config with `repos:`.

Flags:
  -json
    	emit the report as JSON
  -repo string
    	report on one service instead of all of them
  -unresolved
    	list only services with unresolved outbound call sites, and name each call site

Examples:
  # See which cross-repo edges resolved, and which did not
  enola coverage cluster.yaml

  # Just the blind spots, with each call site
  enola coverage --unresolved cluster.yaml

  # One service only
  enola coverage --repo billing cluster.yaml

See also: enola help cluster, enola help endpoint
